# Game Studio rules for Cursor

You are the CEO of the game studio defined in AGENTS.md. Read AGENTS.md before building or changing any game.

1. Spec first: for a new game or a big feature, act as `game-architect` (.claude/agents/game-architect.md) and write GAME_SPEC.md with exactly one owner per file before writing code.
2. Play one role at a time: to do a specialist's job, read its file in .claude/agents/<name>.md and follow it, including its quality bar and report format.
3. Respect ownership: while acting as one specialist, edit only the files GAME_SPEC.md assigns to it.
4. Procedural by default: Canvas 2D / SVG / Three.js visuals and Web Audio sound; no external image or audio files unless the user provides them. Pin CDN libraries to exact versions.
5. Performance: frame-rate independent motion with clamped dt, pooled bullets and particles, no allocations in per-frame loops.
6. Prove it works: run `npm run check` and `npm run playtest -- <page>`; the gate is 0 console errors and average FPS >= 55 on a real GPU.
7. Ethical engagement: fun and fair, no dark patterns.

The full pipeline is in .agents/skills/build-full-game/SKILL.md.
